.\" $NetBSD$
.Dd November 2, 2026
.Dt WSDECORCTL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm wsdecorctl
.Nd select a runtime wscons decoration theme
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl q
.Op Fl f Ar device
.Op Ar theme.conf
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
loads a console decoration without rebuilding or rebooting the kernel.
With no theme file it prints the current display dimensions, decoration type,
and text rectangle.
The default device is
.Pa /dev/ttyE0 .
Setting a theme requires superuser privileges and a writable device.
.Pp
.Fl q
silently skips a missing device or a driver without decoration support.
It does not suppress errors in theme files or failed theme changes.
This is useful during startup on systems with different console drivers.
.Pp
The first implementation supports Newport on sgimips with
.Dv NEWPORT_DECOR
and the vt100 terminal emulator.
Themes apply to every virtual screen on that display.
A change in rows or columns clears existing terminal contents and scrollback,
resets the terminal emulator, updates tty sizes, and sends
.Dv SIGWINCH
so interactive programs can redraw.
Changes that retain the same rows and columns preserve text.
Themes cannot be changed while a screen is in graphics mode or a virtual
screen switch is pending.
.Sh THEME FILES
Each line contains a directive and whitespace-separated arguments.
Blank lines and comments beginning with
.Sq #
are ignored.
Duplicate, unknown, missing, and conflicting directives are errors.
File names cannot contain whitespace or
.Sq # .
.Pp
A gradient theme requires:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
type gradient
top 000000
bottom 008060
.Ed
.Pp
Colours are hexadecimal RGB values without a leading hash.
A solid theme uses
.Dq type solid
and
.Dq color RRGGBB .
Both use the entire display unless a
.Dq viewport x y width height
directive is supplied.
The gradient is anchored to the physical display.
.Pp
An image theme requires:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
type image
image sgiconsole.wsd
viewport 288 176 704 672
.Ed
.Pp
Relative image paths are resolved against the theme file's directory.
Images must match the display height and width; Newport also accepts up to
two extra image columns at the right edge for its VC2 timing variants.
No scaling is performed.
The text rectangle must fit the display and cover a uniform image colour.
Its dimensions are rounded down to whole font cells, with at least 20 columns
and 10 rows.
At an 8 by 16 font the supplied rectangle gives 88 columns and 42 rows.
Black terminal backgrounds reveal the decoration; other terminal colours
remain opaque.
.Pp
The image format is WSDIMG1: eight magic bytes
.Dq WSDIMG1\en ,
four unsigned big-endian 32-bit integers (width, height, palette count,
run count), RGB palette triples, then runs consisting of a big-endian 32-bit
length and one palette index byte.
Runs cover the complete row-major image exactly.
Images are limited to 2048 by 2048 pixels and 223 colours.
The kernel receives only the decoded indices and palette.
.Pp
To convert a PNG on a machine with Python and Pillow:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
python3 /usr/share/wscons/themes/mkwsd.py artwork.png artwork.wsd
.Ed
.Pp
The converter preserves colours exactly and rejects images with transparency
or more than 223 colours; reduce the palette in an image editor first.
.Sh STARTUP
The
.Pa /etc/rc.d/wsdecor
script runs after critical filesystems are mounted and before wscons screen
configuration and login.
The defaults in
.Pa /etc/defaults/rc.conf
are:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
wsdecor=YES
wsdecor_device="/dev/ttyE0"
wsdecor_theme="/usr/share/wscons/themes/framed.conf"
.Ed
.Pp
Override these in
.Pa /etc/rc.conf .
For example, set
.Dq wsdecor_theme=/etc/my-console.conf
and place a theme file there.
Set
.Dq wsdecor=NO
to keep the built-in appearance.
On generic sgimips kernels this is the black-to-green gradient.
The framed startup theme requires a 1280 or 1282 by 1024 display;
a failed load leaves the existing appearance intact.
The optional
.Dv NEWPORT_FRAME
kernel configuration still starts with the compiled-in frame.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
wsdecorctl /usr/share/wscons/themes/initial.conf
wsdecorctl /usr/share/wscons/themes/framed.conf
/etc/rc.d/wsdecor restart
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr wscons 4 ,
.Xr rc.conf 5 ,
.Xr wsconscfg 8 ,
.Xr wsconsctl 8
.Sh LIMITATIONS
The firmware and earliest console output retain their own appearance.
The startup selection requires the userland program, configuration and image
files to be installed alongside the updated kernel.
This first viewport implementation does not support kernels using
.Dv VCONS_DRAW_INTR .
